# Dayflow — Environment Variables
# Every variable below is validated by src/env.ts (@t3-oss/env-nextjs + zod)
# at process startup — a missing/malformed value fails the build or dev
# server immediately with a specific error, not a silent `undefined` deep
# in some route handler. Add new env vars there, not just here.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE — Required
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your Supabase project URL.
# Found at: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → Project URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Public anon key — safe to expose in the browser.
# Found at: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → anon public
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# Service role key — NEVER expose this in the browser or commit to git.
# It bypasses ALL Row Level Security. Server/API routes only.
# Found at: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → service_role (click Reveal)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# Temporary flag to bypass Supabase auth for frontend UI development.
# Set to 'true' to load local mocked sessions, or leave empty/remove for full auth flows.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BYPASS_AUTH=true

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTIFICATIONS — Optional
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Brevo transactional email API (https://api.brevo.com/v3/smtp/email)
# credentials — used by lib/email/mailer.ts (Next.js API routes: employee
# welcome email, leave request submitted/approved/rejected) and by the
# send-notification Edge Function (pg_cron leave escalation). If NOT set,
# both fall back to console.log — zero-config demo path.
#
# BREVO_API_KEY is a v3 API key — Brevo dashboard → Settings → SMTP & API →
# API Keys → Generate a new API key.
# BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL must be a sender verified on the Brevo account
# (Settings → Senders & IP → Senders).
# BREVO_API_KEY=xkeysib-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL=youraddress@yourdomain.com
# BREVO_SENDER_NAME=Dayflow

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Copy this file to .env.local (already gitignored) and fill in real values.
# 2. On Vercel: add each variable under Project Settings → Environment Variables.
#    Mark SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY as "Production, Preview" only (not browser).
# 3. The pg_cron escalation job needs two additional settings set directly in
#    Postgres (not via .env.local). See SUPABASE_SETUP.md Step 8.
# 4. The pg_cron escalation path calls a deployed Edge Function, so
#    BREVO_API_KEY/BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL must also be set as Edge Function
#    secrets (not read from .env.local):
#      supabase functions deploy send-notification
#      supabase secrets set BREVO_API_KEY=... BREVO_SENDER_EMAIL=... BREVO_SENDER_NAME=...
